From 36ad5c86581cf09eec9d091caf8558a3cf88f110 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shircomay <112399495+shircomay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:22:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(audio): echo-cancel the mic against app audio in
 meeting recordings

With speakers instead of headphones, the microphone records the remote
voices a second time, delayed and reverberant, on top of the clean copy that
ScreenCaptureKit delivers. This runs the microphone through
EchoCancellationStage, with the app audio as the reference, before the two
are mixed, so the app audio stays in the recording once.

Opt-in: off by default (`echoCancellation.enabled`), meeting recordings
only, applied from the next recording. With it off, or for microphone-only
and app-audio-only recordings, no stage is created, the timestamp queues stay
disabled and the recording path is the one that was there before.

RecordingSession
- Pops the capture timestamp for every buffer, including ones dropped while
  paused, so the queues never drift against the streams.
- Feeds the app audio to the stage as the reference and mixes the stage's
  output instead of the raw microphone. The stage holds a frame up to 150 ms
  for its reference, so output can lag the input; it never adds or drops a
  microphone sample.
- Applies the adaptive gain to the cleaned samples (deferred gain, see the
  previous commit).
- Flushes held microphone audio on pause and stop, and restarts the stage's
  timeline on pause.
- Once per recording, when both streams have produced a timestamp, checks that
  the two clocks agree. ScreenCaptureKit is assumed to stamp on the host time
  clock like AVAudioTime; if the two streams' timestamps are more than 5 s
  apart that assumption is wrong, the stage falls back to arrival order
  (contiguous mode) and the summary says so.
- A stage that cannot be created bypasses to the existing behaviour.
- Test seams: `consumeSystem` is internal like `consumeMic`,
  `startFakeMeetingForTesting` and `installEchoStageForTesting`.

Settings > Audio gets a "Remove speaker echo from meeting recordings"
toggle, an optional "Save echo-cancellation debug audio" toggle (three
parallel WAVs per meeting, raw mic / aligned reference / cleaned mic, in an
`aec-debug` folder next to the recording; off by default) and a one-line
"Last meeting" summary (echo reduction, estimated delay, reference presence,
or why it was bypassed; numbers only, no user content). EchoCancellationSettings
is an app-wide @StateObject injected into both scenes and registered with the
churn probe; it publishes nothing at audio cadence.

Tests: RecordingSessionEchoCancellationTests (synthetic echo through a fake
meeting session: cancellation vs. the same run without a stage, late and
silent references, no audio lost across pause/resume/stop, clock-mismatch
fallback, deferred gain, debug audio, and that a session without a stage is
untouched) and EchoCancellationSettingsTests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
